 (17 Stat. 368.) Held, that this act did not reinstate rights which were lost before its passage, and that, under the act of December 19th, 1878, (16 Stat. 698), the motion must be refused. Opinion by\nSimpson, C. J.,", "type": "majority", "author": "Simpson, C. J.,"}], "attorneys": ["J. P. Carroll, for appellants. L. F. Youmans, attorney-general, A. J. Norris, contra."], "corrections": "", "head_matter": "No. 1062.\nBlakeley & Copeland v. Frazier.\nApril Term, 1881.\nJuly 30th, 1881.\nJ. P. Carroll, for appellants. L. F. Youmans, attorney-general, A. J. Norris, contra."}, "file_name": "0615-01", "first_page_order": 625, "last_page_order": 625}